### Third-Party Notices & Acknowledgments

This project builds upon and interacts with several upstream components and community research. Respective copyrights and licenses apply:

- **OpenBSD Project**:
  - `configs/install.md` incorporates logic from OpenBSD's installer scripts:
    Copyright (c) 1996 Canonical Software. All rights reserved.
    Redistribution and use in source and binary forms are permitted under standard BSD/ISC terms.
  - OpenBSD kernel source modifications (`scripts/patches/dwc2_split_order_fix.patch` and `scripts/patches/gpiokeys_rawkbd_fix.patch`) are distributed under the ISC License.
  - OpenBSD binaries and sets (`base79.tgz`, `bsd.rd`, etc.) are downloaded directly from official OpenBSD mirrors under ISC / BSD licenses.

- **Joshua Stein (jcs)**:
  - Custom DM250 OpenBSD kernel patches, U-Boot, and device tree (DTB) support:
    https://jcs.org/2026/04/09/openbsd-dm250
    Binaries and scripts are fetched from upstream sources during installation under respective ISC / GPL licenses.
  - Wi-Fi NVRAM configuration parameter template for Broadcom AP6212 / BCM43430 (`configs/brcmfmac43430-sdio.rockchip,pomera-dm250.txt`).

- **4noha**:
  - Research, kernel patches (`scripts/patches/bcmbt_delay_2s.patch`, `scripts/patches/rkdrm_wsdisplay_smode.patch` under the ISC License), mlterm-fb patches (`scripts/patches/mlterm-fb-dm250-shadowfb.patch` under the MIT License), Bluetooth PAN tethering research, and power management concepts for Pomera DM250:
    Copyright (c) 2026 4noha
    https://github.com/4noha/openbsd-pomera-dm250

- **ichinomoto**:
  - Pioneering research and the EKESETE eMMC backup tool, which established safe experimental procedures on physical Pomera DM250 hardware.

- **Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.**:
  - Bootloader miniloader and DDR initialization binaries (`rkbin`) are fetched directly from Rockchip's official repositories.
